{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7","id":1461167,"title":"Combining Clans to get back to 7","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-23T23:40:11-07:00","id":1461167,"title":"Combining Clans to get back to 7","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">So, this is a crazy idea, but it might be kinda fun. Also, it\u2019s different from the pro vs con V5 debates we often get here. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">I was thinking it might be interesting to reverse the proliferation of Clans that we got in V:tM after 1st edition. Back when there were still 7 Clans. So I decided to combine the Clans and major bloodlines in V:tM into 7. Sounds kinda like Requiem right? Well, that isn\u2019t my intention, since those Clans are broad archetypes and these are more specific sets of culture, tradition, organization, etc.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Anyway, first I\u2019ll start with how the Clans combine and the Disciplines the new Clans get. I decided to go with 4 Disciplines per Clan instead of 3, to capture important powers or themes from the component Clans. I tried to aim for each standard Discipline to appear about 3 times.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Toreador+Malkavian: Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate, Presence</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Tzimisce+Giovanni+Gangrel: Animalism, Fortitude, Potence, Protean</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Ventrue+Salubri: Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude, Presence</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Tremere+Cappadocian: Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude, Necromancy</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Lasombra+Baali+Setites: Dominate, Obfuscate, Obtenebration, Potence</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Nosferatu+Assamites: Animalism, Celerity, Obfuscate, Potence</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Brujah+Ravnos: Animalism, Celerity, Potence, Presence</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Now for a more detailed (yet still brief) description of these composite Clans:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Malkavian</b> (Toreador/Malkavian)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Malkavian Clan are a Clan of passionate artists and visionaries. They pursue new passions, new ideas, new ways to create art and beauty. The are also plagued by obsessive behavior and even madness, perusing their endeavors with such zeal that they destroy themselves and those around them. Beyond mere art and creativity, the Malkavians are known for their supernatural insights, such as the ability to catch glimpses of the future.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Disciplines: Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate, Presence</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Weakness: the Malkavian each have a single permanent derangement, though this malady almost always relates to an obsession with some form of art, hedonistic pleasure, or creative pursuit.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Basarab</b> (Tzimisce/Giovanni/Gangrel)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Basarab Clan still hold to the ancient ways when they were feudal lords who ruled openly over peasants and whose wealth was measured in acres and not numbers of a bank account. The Basarab are like dominant predators, their domain is their\u2019s alone and all within must submit or die. For millennia their progenitor Clan was served by Revenant ghoul families, until at last one great family and its vampiric master usurped the Clan and they became the Basarab. A large percentage of this Clan are drawn from other such families created by the Basarab or their precursors: Bratovitch, Zantosa, Rossellini, Obertus, Dunsirn, and so on. They also make frequent use of ghoul servants, both human and animal. With the decline of feudal power, some Basarab vampires have been able to transition to modern life and live deep in the wilderness away from town or city.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Disciplines: Animalism, Fortitude, Potence, Protean</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Weakness: As the Gangrel weakness, though each time they DON\u2019T sleep within their native soul they also gain an animal feature.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Valere</b> (Ventrue/Salubri)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Valere are nobles among the kindred, though not just rulers, they are philosopher kings who see it as their duty to bring peace to their undead race and to limit the worst exploitation\u2019s of others of their kind. The Valere seek to lead vampires, not merely for the sake of power, but to guide them to a better path, to protect humans from vampiric oppression and predation, and even to seek out a way to personally reach Golconda and guide other vampires there as well.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Disciplines: Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude, Presence</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Weakness: As the Ventrue, they must select a certain type of blood. Though they may drink others kinds of blood, they must drink 2 blood points to gain 1 point of nourishment. Furthermore, the Valere are loath to drink the blood of non-consenting humans, and may not do so unless they spend a point of Willpower, which allows them to drink their blood for a scene.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Tremere</b> (Tremere/Cappadocian)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Much like the Tremere of canon, these were a group of magic users who used a ritual to grant themselves immortality: becoming vampires. Though these were necromancers whose powers over death and undeath allowed them to become vampires. Instead of gargoyle servants, they use zombies and spirits against their enemies.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Disciplines: Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude, Necromancy</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Weakness: As the Cappadocian weakness, they are pale and lifeless, unable to use blush of life. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Azaneali</b> (Lasombra/Baali/Setites)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Azaneali are the black priests of the kindred. They serve demonic entities of darkness and the abyss, sometimes in the form of Satan or Set, sometimes something more Cthonic in form. The Azaneali believe in embracing what they see as their true vampiric nature: creatures of darkness, of evil. From a more secular prospective, they believe that might makes right, they mercy only fosters weakness, and even those Azaneali who don\u2019t openly venerate dark gods embrace a Darwinian attitude that can justify terrible acts. The Azaneali believe that it is the right of the strong to rule and seek positions of power over human and vampire alike, using such power to guide others towards darkness.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Disciplines: Dominate, Obtenebration, Obfuscate, Potence</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Orlok</b> (Nosferatu/Assamites)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Like the Nosferatu of canon, these vampires were cursed with terrible ugliness. Though in addition to becoming masterful spies from being forced to hide from kindred and kind alike, but also became assassins without peer. Being isolated from other vampires allows them to be rather more cold blooded in slaying their kin, and the tight knit unity of the Clan allows them to spread information about who needs their serves as spies or assassins. Some Nosferatu believe that their curse will be lifted if all other vampires are eradicated, and so seek to destroy other vampires, though most spy or kill for more tangible rewards. </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Disciplines: Animalism, Celerity, Obfuscate, Potence</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Weakness: as the Nosferatu weakness</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Ravnos</b> (Ravnos/Brujah)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Ravnos Clan are a Clan that seeks personal liberty and freedoms. Often they are nomadic, traveling from place to place, breaking laws of kindred or kind as is convenient. Those who prefer to stay in a certain region or city will invariably seek to oppose authority figures, oppressive laws, or other restrictions them. While there are a fair number of Ravnos in the Camarilla, they frequently support Anarchs or (for older wiser members of the Clan) seek to work within the system to undermine authority or even rising to power by promising \u201cpower to the people.\u201d The Ravnos are over-represented among itinerant groups - like bikers, Romani, shepherds, and the like - though this is hardly universal. </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Disciplines: Animalism, Celerity, Potence, Presence</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Weakness: the Ravnos are compelled to travel. Staying in one location for too long causes them to become more short tempered and irritable until the Beast rises to the surface and becomes uncontrollable. Each day after the first spent in the same location raises the difficulty to resist frenzy by 1. This continues to increase until they spend a week away from that location.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, those are some of my crazy ideas. Any thoughts?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 09-24-2021, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T02:06:00-07:00","id":1461177,"title":"","content":"cool but Isnt this what requiem effectively is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T07:43:18-07:00","id":1461213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461177#post1461177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cool but Isnt this what requiem effectively is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, kind of. Though I think its different in at least one important regard. The Clans I have are more like groups that have their own history, structure, organization, relations with allied or rival Clans. Requiem Clans are more like archetypes, a set of powers and weaknesses, and the organization comes from belonging to the Carhians, Invictus, etc.<br /> <br /> So, yes, there are similarities, but differences as well. I suppose the above Clans could be compared to Requiem bloodlines since they have 4 Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T08:16:15-07:00","id":1461218,"title":"","content":"Personally I've considered fusing the Tremere and the Nosferatu, making them basically the D&amp;D Hag clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T08:30:36-07:00","id":1461221,"title":"","content":"Requiem clans do have hierarchies. Or at least can. Some are more organized than others. <i>World of Darkness: Chicago</i> gave the local Ventrue a very centralized hierarchy called &quot;the Structure&quot; whose name I've actually stolen/repurposed for the Ventrue clan's organization in my Masquerade games. The interplay there between clan and covenant positions was interesting, as the city's Ventrue prince was top dog among the Invictus but merely considered &quot;a liaison&quot; to the Invictus by his fellow Ventrue, and implied to only have a middling place in the clan hierarchy.<br /> <br /> The late 1e clanbooks, which were basically 2e books with the serial numbers filed off, expanded the five clans and gave them tons of history, culture, and depth beyond the five archetypes. At the same time, GMs could use as much or as little of that as they wanted, and could limit history/culture/depth to the covenants if they preferred clans to play a lesser role. Requiem has always been great at the toolbox approach.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are some neat ideas and marriages of concepts here, but I agree you're reinventing the wheel if you're wanting to winnow down the number of clans in the game. I'd probably just use the Requiem clans with bloodlines to cover some of the more &quot;exotic&quot; or niche clan concepts like Salubri and Giovanni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T10:23:05-07:00","id":1461236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461218#post1461218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I've considered fusing the Tremere and the Nosferatu, making them basically the D&amp;D Hag clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, that would be pretty cool. Now I have to rearrange everything <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe Animalism, Auspex, Obfuscate, Thaumaturgy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461221#post1461221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem clans do have hierarchies. Or at least can. Some are more organized than others. <i>World of Darkness: Chicago</i> gave the local Ventrue a very centralized hierarchy called &quot;the Structure&quot; whose name I've actually stolen/repurposed for the Ventrue clan's organization in my Masquerade games. The interplay there between clan and covenant positions was interesting, as the city's Ventrue prince was top dog among the Invictus but merely considered &quot;a liaison&quot; to the Invictus by his fellow Ventrue, and implied to only have a middling place in the clan hierarchy.<br /> <br /> The late 1e clanbooks, which were basically 2e books with the serial numbers filed off, expanded the five clans and gave them tons of history, culture, and depth beyond the five archetypes. At the same time, GMs could use as much or as little of that as they wanted, and could limit history/culture/depth to the covenants if they preferred clans to play a lesser role. Requiem has always been great at the toolbox approach.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are some neat ideas and marriages of concepts here, but I agree you're reinventing the wheel if you're wanting to winnow down the number of clans in the game. I'd probably just use the Requiem clans with bloodlines to cover some of the more &quot;exotic&quot; or niche clan concepts like Salubri and Giovanni.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read any of the Requiem Clan books, so I'm not that familiar with what they did with Requiem after the first few books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T11:18:31-07:00","id":1461242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461236#post1461236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, that would be pretty cool. Now I have to rearrange everything <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe Animalism, Auspex, Obfuscate, Thaumaturgy?</div> </div> </div> </div>A D&amp;D Hag clan is a cool idea, but so is your injection of a bit of Assamite into the Nosferatu. Sneaking Celerity into their in-clan disciplines is a brilliant move, because super-speed is one of the most noticeable vampiric powers that Count Orlok has in Murnau's <i>Nosferatu.</i> Your Nosferatu-Assamite blend feels wonderfully archetypal to me.<br /> <br /> The Basarab are another top-notch mixture. Very <i>Requiem</i>-esque -- isn't Dracula a Gangrel in <i>Requiem?</i> -- but that's hardly a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T11:40:36-07:00","id":1461246,"title":"","content":"Another thing that I like is that you've clearly made an effort to spread out the disciplines between the clans in a balanced sort of way. What often happens when fans or even published writers rearrange the clans is that they assign disciplines purely based on clan concepts and end up favoring one or two disciplines noticeably over the others. Here, however, you have 11 disciplines, seven of which are shared among three clans. That's pretty great.<br /> <br /> What I would do is bite the bullet and remove the remaining unique disciplines. What little Obtenebration has to offer can be safely folded into Obfuscate (something that I think V5 should have done instead of the clunky Obtenebration-Necromancy hybrid the edition went with). Protean is such a classic that it ought to be shared among at least two clans, but I'm not sure which of the others apart from the Basarab would be a good fit.<br /> <br /> Combining the clans into a smaller set is a fun exercise, at any rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T12:21:06-07:00","id":1461254,"title":"","content":"I've tried to do this multiple times. Here is my take<br /> <br /> Toreador/Brujah - Punks and artistes that are closest to mortals.<br /> Malkavian - Just like they are in VtM <br /> Ventrue/Lasombra - Lasombra are basically just a darker shade of Ventrue already<br /> Gangrel/Tzimisce/Setite/Ravnos - Animalistic and noble - Think Dark Ages Tzimisce rather than Sabbat Tzimisce. The Setites and Ravnos are part of this clan but act more as bloodlines.<br /> Tremere/Cappadocian/Giovanni - Giovanni slew Cappadocius but were unable to get rid of the entire clan. They adopted the Tremere into their clan after the diablerie of Saulot.<br /> Assamite - Just like they are in VtM<br /> Nosferatu - Just like they are in VtM<br /> <br /> My main problem with this is the Gangrel/Tzimisce/Setite/Ravnos clusterfuck. Gangrel can be combined with any of the three other clans but it's hard to combine Ravnos with Tzimisce or Tzimisce with Setites<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T12:38:55-07:00","id":1461257,"title":"","content":"Oh damn, I actually really like that Basarab Clan idea actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T14:09:43-07:00","id":1461267,"title":"","content":"I'd just use the original 7 Camarilla clans. They provide the most diversity and can easily include any kind of concept that would fit into the Sabbat and Independent clans.<br /> <br /> The independent clans are essentially gimmick clans designed to fit a very specific role. They've been subsequently developed to be more than that, but only by covering territory already covered by others. The Sabbat clans have stronger concepts, but are essentially just darker archetypes of those found in the Camarilla. To a large degree unfortunately, all the non-Cam clans were essentially defined by their unique signature Discipline, and the official game has slowly realized that over the years and tried to fix that in various ways.<br /> <br /> Really the only Camarilla clan that would need to change would be Tremere since they are so lore specific and dependent on a strict hierarchy. Opening them up to be an older and more open clan would solve that, so presumably using elements of the Salubri and Cappadocians could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T15:50:44-07:00","id":1461276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461267#post1461267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really the only Camarilla clan that would need to change would be Tremere since they are so lore specific and dependent on a strict hierarchy. Opening them up to be an older and more open clan would solve that, so presumably using elements of the Salubri and Cappadocians could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me the best change in this sense would be to use the Tzimisce Kolduns with elements of the Cappadocians and Salubri. Auspex and Thamaturgy (maybe with the option to change it to a &quot;bloodline gimmick&quot; to use the other disciplines as schools of magic), I'd get Animalism instead of Fortitude or Dominate, personally. To me the ability of talking with the creatures of the Earth and commanding them have more of the feeling of &quot;magic&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T19:12:20-07:00","id":1461290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461246#post1461246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that I like is that you've clearly made an effort to spread out the disciplines between the clans in a balanced sort of way. What often happens when fans or even published writers rearrange the clans is that they assign disciplines purely based on clan concepts and end up favoring one or two disciplines noticeably over the others. Here, however, you have 11 disciplines, seven of which are shared among three clans. That's pretty great.<br /> <br /> What I would do is bite the bullet and remove the remaining unique disciplines. What little Obtenebration has to offer can be safely folded into Obfuscate (something that I think V5 should have done instead of the clunky Obtenebration-Necromancy hybrid the edition went with). Protean is such a classic that it ought to be shared among at least two clans, but I'm not sure which of the others apart from the Basarab would be a good fit.<br /> <br /> Combining the clans into a smaller set is a fun exercise, at any rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about eliminating special Disciplines and I did to some degree. I felt torn about it because some of those Disciplines are iconic and others are gimmicky. Protean is iconic. Maybe Obtenebration could be Obfuscate, though they seem different in many ways. I felt really tempted to give my Brujah/Ravnos combo Chimerstry to emulate the Lost Boys and their illusion powers. I felt a little constrained by having to combine Clans, include all of the canon Clans, balance out Disciplines, and so on. I could potentially have just created entirely new Clans that fulfilled the rolled I wanted, but I also wanted to include all of the old Clans, since it seems interesting.<br /> <br /> I think that having Tzimisce and Gangrel (along with other Clans) as 2 separate Clans, where both could have Protean, would be cool. Protean becomes a special Discipline because the two Clans that might have it were combined. The above arrangement is just one of many that I tried, some have two different Clans with Protean. <br /> <br /> I think that the Nosferatu and Assamites fit together pretty seemlessly. In fact, the Nosferatu have always had great potential as assassins, so it\u2019s not that big of a stretch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461254#post1461254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've tried to do this multiple times. Here is my take<br /> <br /> Toreador/Brujah - Punks and artistes that are closest to mortals.<br /> Malkavian - Just like they are in VtM<br /> Ventrue/Lasombra - Lasombra are basically just a darker shade of Ventrue already<br /> Gangrel/Tzimisce/Setite/Ravnos - Animalistic and noble - Think Dark Ages Tzimisce rather than Sabbat Tzimisce. The Setites and Ravnos are part of this clan but act more as bloodlines.<br /> Tremere/Cappadocian/Giovanni - Giovanni slew Cappadocius but were unable to get rid of the entire clan. They adopted the Tremere into their clan after the diablerie of Saulot.<br /> Assamite - Just like they are in VtM<br /> Nosferatu - Just like they are in VtM<br /> <br /> My main problem with this is the Gangrel/Tzimisce/Setite/Ravnos clusterfuck. Gangrel can be combined with any of the three other clans but it's hard to combine Ravnos with Tzimisce or Tzimisce with Setites</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. You actually included several of the the things I did in different versions I tried and I still feel conflicted about what combinations are best. Ventrue/Lasombra and Toreador/Brujah were both some of the combos I used most in some of my models.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461257#post1461257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh damn, I actually really like that Basarab Clan idea actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I think it\u2019s a cool idea as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461267#post1461267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just use the original 7 Camarilla clans. They provide the most diversity and can easily include any kind of concept that would fit into the Sabbat and Independent clans.<br /> <br /> The independent clans are essentially gimmick clans designed to fit a very specific role. They've been subsequently developed to be more than that, but only by covering territory already covered by others. The Sabbat clans have stronger concepts, but are essentially just darker archetypes of those found in the Camarilla. To a large degree unfortunately, all the non-Cam clans were essentially defined by their unique signature Discipline, and the official game has slowly realized that over the years and tried to fix that in various ways.<br /> <br /> Really the only Camarilla clan that would need to change would be Tremere since they are so lore specific and dependent on a strict hierarchy. Opening them up to be an older and more open clan would solve that, so presumably using elements of the Salubri and Cappadocians could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, where is the fun in that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though, honestly you make a good point. I do think that the Sabbat Clans have character, but the Lasombra could just be Ventrue with a certain style and attitude, while the Tzimisce could be Gangrel who are more politically inclined or Ventrue who are more rural. The Independent Clans do rely pretty heavily on the gimmick Discipline and ethnic stereotype. I think that the Giovanni are an exception, but they\u2019re also very similar to the Tremere. <br /> <br /> So, I suppose I could just use some system far closer to the original 7, but, well, I wanted to make something different to be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T20:00:49-07:00","id":1461292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461290#post1461290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought about eliminating special Disciplines and I did to some degree. I felt torn about it because some of those Disciplines are iconic and others are gimmicky.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could keep your spread and just rethink what role Protean plays. It is a &quot;special discipline&quot; only in the sense that somehow the original writers only managed to give this extremely iconic vampiric power to the Gangrel. But I can easily picture in the same structure you built on OP the three clans with &quot;special disciplines&quot; all having Protean instead. With the precise exception of the Gangrel they are all clans with at least some &quot;magical&quot; background and you have some elements of Protean in Mortis (acquiring aspects of the dead or the living), Serpentis (it is basically snake-themed Protean), Obtenebration (extending shadowy tendrils or changing into shadow) and some Infernal Investments (Daimonion is just Edgy Dominate).<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'll be the one to say it, but I didn't liked the Basarab keeping the Giovanni Treason as a lore. That's the only thing I didn't liked about them. And I would change some weaknesses:<br /> - Basarab, as written, will encourage them to live distant from their land as sleeping there accelerates their transformation. Do the opposite, instead of sleeping in your native soil giving you more animal features, sleeping <u>outside</u> of your native soil may be <u>the only</u> way to gain animal features, so staying at home stabilizes you.<br /> - Azaneali, you didn't gave them a weakness, but I imagine that it will be the Setite one?<br /> - Ravnos, if it stay increasing every night it will just make it completely impossible for them to stay in a single place, it is absurdly strong. And since it is also simple to get rid off, instead of having the two kinds of characters, nomads and hotheads, you'll have nomads and Masquerade compromises. Either cap it at +1 or make it take a week to increase after the first +1 and cap at +2, that way characters that really want to be more sedentary won't be too pressed and will actually (un)live with the penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T20:31:06-07:00","id":1461297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461292#post1461292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could keep your spread and just rethink what role Protean plays. It is a &quot;special discipline&quot; only in the sense that somehow the original writers only managed to give this extremely iconic vampiric power to the Gangrel. But I can easily picture in the same structure you built on OP the three clans with &quot;special disciplines&quot; all having Protean instead. With the precise exception of the Gangrel they are all clans with at least some &quot;magical&quot; background and you have some elements of Protean in Mortis (acquiring aspects of the dead or the living), Serpentis (it is basically snake-themed Protean), Obtenebration (extending shadowy tendrils or changing into shadow) and some Infernal Investments (Daimonion is just Edgy Dominate).<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'll be the one to say it, but I didn't liked the Basarab keeping the Giovanni Treason as a lore. That's the only thing I didn't liked about them. And I would change some weaknesses:<br /> - Basarab, as written, will encourage them to live distant from their land as sleeping there accelerates their transformation. Do the opposite, instead of sleeping in your native soil giving you more animal features, sleeping <u>outside</u> of your native soil may be <u>the only</u> way to gain animal features, so staying at home stabilizes you.<br /> - Azaneali, you didn't gave them a weakness, but I imagine that it will be the Setite one?<br /> - Ravnos, if it stay increasing every night it will just make it completely impossible for them to stay in a single place, it is absurdly strong. And since it is also simple to get rid off, instead of having the two kinds of characters, nomads and hotheads, you'll have nomads and Masquerade compromises. Either cap it at +1 or make it take a week to increase after the first +1 and cap at +2, that way characters that really want to be more sedentary won't be too pressed and will actually (un)live with the penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see Protean very easily applying to other kinds of shapeshifting. Serpentis basically is Protean and Protean makes a nice alternative to Vicissitude. For some of the other Disciplines, it might be a bit more questionable. Maybe a more thorough reworking of Disciplines would help. You\u2019re right about Daimoinon, no need for that with mind affecting Disciplines.<br /> <br /> I wasn\u2019t sure about keeping the Basarab family betrayal either. Though if we go with the medieval Basarab family as the heart of the Clan, it seems like some kind of change related to that might have to happen. Though I suppose that the Basarab family could be ancient and only reveal themselves in the Middle Ages. I actually mistyped my Basarab weakness. I meant for them to gain animal features when they don\u2019t sleep in native soil, so we are on the same page their.<br /> <br /> Yes, I think that the Azaneali weakness should be the same as the Setite weakness. Though perhaps some weakness to faith might be interesting as well.<br /> <br /> As for the Ravnos weakness, I think you make a good point. I based in on the V5 Ravnos weakness, where they have problems that accumulate by the day. Though actual nomads don\u2019t have a new sleeping place every night. They have a new sleeping place every week or month. So a more slow building penalty might be better. Maybe some non-linear accumulation of penalties. A penalty after a week, then after a month, then after a year.<br /> <br /> I wanted to reply to your other post as well. I like the combination of Animalism and Thaumaturgy/Sorcery. Kind of like the Rafastio or Lhiannan. It has a pagan sort of vibe. I didn\u2019t do that above, but I think it would be a cool combination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 09-24-2021, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T21:29:31-07:00","id":1461301,"title":"","content":"My mergers would probably be as follows;<br /> <br /> General - all common disciplines can be learned instinctively; disciplines cost x5 for clan, x6 for other common disciplines and x7 for special disciplines.<br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel/Ravnos/Old Clan Tzmisce: </b> outsiders and border lords; disciplines - Animalism, Obfuscate, Protean; weakness - has obsessive attachment to something (a people, place, activity) and suffer +1 diff to all Self-Control checks per night you are separated from it.<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue/Lasombra/Giovanni: </b> imperious masters of the living and the dead; disciplines - Dominate (mental control), Potence (physical control), Necromancy (control of the dead); weakness - increased difficulty with all actions related to emotions.<br /> <br /> <b>Brujah/Assamites:</b> warrior philosophers; disciplines - Auspex, Celerity, Potence; weakness - increased difficulty with frenzy checks for each blood point spent during the night.<br /> <br /> <b>Toreador/Malkavian:</b> sensualists/hedonists; disciplines- Auspex, Celerity, Presence; have an addiction (exacerbated from their mortal life) and lose willpower each night they do not partake of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere/Setite:</b> a merger of Gnostic and Hermetic philosophy; disciplines - Fortitude (resist change by others), Protean (embrace change of self), Sorcery (transform the world). weakness - they cannot enslave others with the blood bond (some believe this is psychosomatic and related to Clan\u2019s focus on breaking free of the trap that is the mortal world). Instead of Saulot, Tremere attempted to diablerize Set in order to learn more of the origins of Hermetic magic (believed be from Thoth/Hermes Trimagestus and Isis), but instead of being locked in constant struggle, the two beings merged into a Rebus.<br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu/Cappadocian/Samedi:</b> reclusive and hidden students of life and death; disciplines - Animalism, Obfuscate, Necromancy; weakness - monstrous appearance.<br /> <br /> <b>Baali/Tzimisce/Nagaraja:</b> the monsters under the bed and creators of horrors; disciplines - Daimonion, Necromancy, Vicissitude; weakness - has a victim preference and must spend willpower to feed from non-victims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T13:38:29-07:00","id":1461415,"title":"","content":"Brujah + Toreador = The &quot;social predator&quot; clan who are the most likely to interact with and take part in the night time cultures of the living, driven by dark passions and prone to fixations on their subjects of interest. (Celerity, Potence, Presence) <br /> <br /> Ventrue + Losambra = The &quot;high lords of the night&quot; clan who see themselves as the natural leaders of vampire society by right of personal strength and perseverance, prone to extreme stubbornness and a need to control. (Dominate, Fortutude, Potence)<br /> <br /> Gangrel + Ravnos = The &quot;nomadic outlaw&quot; clan who refuse to bend the knee to anyone who can't earn their respect, seen as wild and almost uncontrollable by others, driven by their baser instincts. (Animalism, Fortitude, Protean)<br /> <br /> Tremere + Setite = The &quot;corrupt witch&quot; clan who are cliquish and power hungry, having originated from a mortal sorcerer who turned themselves into vampires and maintaining their mastery of dark magics, devoted to their founder as an unliving god, but cursed by the pact the clan founder made. (Dominate, Presence, Thaumaturgy/Blood-Magic)<br /> <br /> Nosferatu + Tzimisce = The &quot;creepy outsider&quot; clan who often keep to themselves in their own hidden and well defended territories where they pursue their own arcane and uncanny interests, their presence often making others uncomfortable. (Animalism, Auspex, Obfuscate)<br /> <br /> Malkavian + Assamite = The &quot;exotic mystic&quot; clan who delve into the hidden corners and forbidden crevices of the world in search of esoteric truths and strange enlightenment, seeing the world much differently than others and driven by strange obsessions only they understand. (Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate)<br /> <br /> Cappadocian + Salubri = The &quot;haunted necromancer&quot; clan who walk with one foot in the underworld and deal with the souls of both the living and the dead, often having trouble distinguishing between the two and perpetually surrounded by restless dead. (Auspex, Fortitude, Necromancy) <br /> <br /> That's just what occurs off the top of my head. If I tried, I could probably come up with a unique Discipline for each (Eros, Command, Protean, Hemourgy, etc.).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T17:23:53-07:00","id":1461442,"title":"","content":"I'll try my take here. I'm going for some strange mix here and there on purpose, but still in a way that I want to keep most of what I like in each on the final result. For the Disciplines I completely ditched the usual spreads, kept to the idea of 4 per clan, and redistributed them based on some goals:<br /> - I don't want gimmick disciplines on the in-clans (I have no problem with them as out-clans);<br /> - No magic in-clan;<br /> - Every discipline appears at least 3 times;<br /> - The most varied spreads possible, two clans shouldn't differentiate by less than 2 disciplines;<br /> - One Physical Discipline per clan if possible;<br /> - Possibility of getting any combination of two disciplines as in-clan if you want (I failed, but got close).<br /> <br /> Here I present my current result. I'm not entirely satisfied as I couldn't combine yet Animalism + Presence, Dominate + Obfuscate or Obfuscate + Presence, and I feel that two clans with Dominate + Presence isn't right, but for now I couldn't get around it in a satisfactory way. I'm still working on weaknesses, too.<br /> <br /> - Assamite + Cappadocian (The Scholars)<br /> Disciplines - Auspex, Fortitude, Obfuscate, Protean<br /> Possibly the most organized clan, focused on researching the mysteries of the world with patience. Their oldest elders are theologians, and the most significant of its factions are centered in two great hidden temples, fighting over interpretations of God, life, death, and the meaning of the undead condition. But they're not priests in the end, and they foment research in the nature of the cosmos in whatever form it takes. The clan have astrophysicists, archaeologists, philosophers, spies.<br /> <br /> - Nosferatu + Tzimisce (The Monsters)<br /> Disciplines - Animalism, Obfuscate, Potence, Protean<br /> Linked to the land and to old stories, members of this clan have a hard time taking part on mortal society for long periods, even for the standards of the Kindred. They are the goblins and the hags, they're the strange fairies with strange rules about them, they're the embodiment of old legends about creatures decidedly not human in appearance or demeanor. They do encounter others in their own terms, hiding in shadows or receiving guests in their isolated domains, and form a complex society.<br /> <br /> - Salubri + Setite (The Priests)<br /> Disciplines - Auspex, Celerity, Presence, Protean<br /> Given the insight in the souls of others and the power to stir them, those vampires can wield all forms of faith when they put their minds into it, for good or ill. Many are religious themselves, and that personal faith counts a lot to determine what they'll do with the souls they collect. Some are healers of body or mind. Some are prophets. Some are avengers. And some serve dark gods that only want to drown the world in chaos. Some in the end serve no god but themselves .<br /> <br /> - Gangrel + Lasombra (The Survivors)<br /> Disciplines - Animalism, Celerity, Fortitude, Obfuscate<br /> Once upon a time the founder of this clan wandered the wilds looking for ways to never die. It found four answers: flee danger whenever possible and strike your prey before it reacts, hide to never be found by enemy, harden your flesh to withstand the unavoidable blows and trust only the instincts of animals, never the reason of humans, then explore the ends of the world and the darkness beyond so you'll learn everything that can harm you. Most of the clan think of it as a useful coward.<br /> <br /> - Malkavian + Tremere (The Mystics)<br /> Disciplines - Auspex, Animalism, Dominate, Potence<br /> While some want to know the workings of the cosmos or the will of the gods, others wanted to thwart it and shift the universe to their own designs. Knowledge must be tempered with wisdom if one wants to avoid the consequences of transgression, but humility was anathema to the first elders of the clan. To this day their childer toil under the curses they brought, some seeking now for the wisdom to alleviate their suffering, others pressing even more on the outskirts of reallity.<br /> <br /> - Ventrue + Toreador (The Shepherds) - Dominate, Fortitude, Presence, Protean<br /> Every vampire depend on mortals, mingle with them, guide and nurture for their own interests. But no clan is so prepared for the task of controlling mortal masses. Able to go wherever they want and face whatever awaits there for the opportunity to bring down the will of their targets and infiltrate clusters of beggars and houses of aristocrats with the same ease, they have the power of the very world Kindred live in and need to feed from.<br /> <br /> - Brujah + Ravnos (The Idealists)<br /> Disciplines - Celerity, Dominate, Potence, Presence<br /> <i>I'm too tired to continue now, seriously. Something something, Brujah as philosophers and Mayaparisatya, 'cause original Path of Paradox is dumb.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T20:50:08-07:00","id":1461472,"title":"","content":"Wow, those are some cool Clan combinations. This is a fun thought exercise. Let me try my hand at a second grouping:<br /> <br /> Lasombra/Brujah: Celerity, Obtenebration, Potence, Presence<br /> Weakness: because of their violent disposition, they are quicker to anger especially at disrespect from underlings, suffering a +1 difficulty to resist frenzy. They are also more vulnerable to sunlight than other vampires, taking an extra level of damage from sunlight.<br /> These are the brutal darwinians of the vampiric world. They seek to rule not to guide vampire to some greater good or out of a sense of duty, but because it is right for the strong to rule the weak. They don\u2019t necessarily respect in law or hierarchy that they perceive as protecting weak rulers, so often this Clan ends up as revolutionaries. Just as often, when they have the power, they cruelly crush dissent.<br /> <br /> Tremere/Malkavian: Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate, Sorcery<br /> Weakness: they have a derangement, as Malkavians<br /> Once an order of wizards who sought immortality, they transformed themselves into vampires, much like canon Tremere. Though their pursuit of the d\u2019ordine arts of magic and their contact with chaotic forces has taken a toll on their minds, driving them insane. Often this insanity takes the form of obsessions with knowledge or power.<br /> <br /> Toreador/Setite/Ravnos: Auspex, Celerity, Fortitude, Presence<br /> Weakness: Like the Ravnos, this Clan has a single vice, almost always related to some kind of hedonistic pleasure.<br /> This is a Clan of hedonists and pleasure seekers. They love their vampiric state and fill every moment with beauty, pleasure, and degeneracy. While they are active in the arts, they are just as likely to be debauched nobles. Many also believe in tempting others to indulge in their vices and many of the their herds and ghouls are as much addicted to vice as they.<br /> <br /> Giovanni/Cappadocian/Baali: Fortitude, Necromancy, Potence, Presence<br /> Weakness: they are pale and cannot use blush of life. Furthermore, they are affected by symbols of faith or goodness brandished by anyone with a humanity of 6 or more - count as people as having one additional point of True Faith. An ancient inbred family of demon worshipers were transformed first into ghouls, then many were embraced by a vampire Clan. This family was able to overthrow their parent Clan with the help of demonic masters and become a full Clan themselves. Their dark rituals involve speaking to and commanding the souls of the damned, sometimes even ripping the souls out of still Irving victims. The original family line still exists as revenants and forms the core of the Clan, though they sometimes embrace others as well.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu/Salubri: Animalism, Auspex, Obfuscate, Potence<br /> Weakness: These vampires are ugly, but not to the degree of the Nosferatu. They may never raise their Appearance above 1. If they feed on a non-consenting human, they gain the full Nosferatu weakness for a number of nights equal to the blood points consumed.<br /> This is a Clan of vampires cursed to ugliness, though in being so cursed many have found redemption. They are a Clan of scholars, philosophers, and seekers of knowledge. They often accumulate vast libraries in their subterranean abodes, a feat now facilitated by modern technology. They sometimes sell their knowledge to others, though they seldom do so if they believe that the knowledge or information will be used for wicked ends.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce/Ventrue: Animalism, Dominate, Fortitude, Protean<br /> Weakness: They gain only half the blood points when they drink for a source that is not \u201ctheirs\u201d - meaning their herd, their ghouls, their animals, their childer, their slaves, their subjects, etc.<br /> These vampires are lords, of land, of people, of animals. Still like feudal lords of old, they possess a territory and all within is theirs, at least this is what they wish and seek out. By far the most conservative of Clans, they still rule large domains with an iron fist. Though harsh, they are also fair and honorable, having a strong sense of Noblesse Oblige. Some of these vampires have territories in the wilds, like a territorial predatory. Others rule neighborhoods like a gang. Many still live in ancestral castles with farmers working the land. The power of this Clan has waned in recent years.<br /> <br /> Gangrel/Assamites: Animalism, Celerity, Obfuscate, Protean<br /> Weakness: these predators are filled with ravenous hunger for blood. Each blood point below 10 causes them to gain an animalistic feature. Their Social attributes have a maximum of their current blood pool. At zero blood, they are bestial in appearance and behavior - breaking the Masquerade. Furthermore, they have a +1 penalty to difficulties to resist hunger frenzies.<br /> This is a Clan of hunters and animalistic predators. Like predators, they love the thrill of the hunt and catching their prey, be it man or beast. In the wilderness they prey upon animals. In the urban jungles, humans are their prey. Some even go for big game - vampires or other supernatural creatures. Because of their skill at hunting and killing, these vampires are frequently employed as assassins, either for pay or to gain status within kindred society.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I feel like I\u2019m still not quite able to abandon the signature Disciplines entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 09-26-2021, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T05:30:22-07:00","id":1461942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Toreador+Malkavian: Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate, Presence<br /> Tzimisce+Giovanni+Gangrel: Animalism, Fortitude, Potence, Protean<br /> Ventrue+Salubri: Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude, Presence<br /> Tremere+Cappadocian: Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude, Necromancy<br /> Lasombra+Baali+Setites: Dominate, Obfuscate, Obtenebration, Potence<br /> Nosferatu+Assamites: Animalism, Celerity, Obfuscate, Potence<br /> Brujah+Ravnos: Animalism, Celerity, Potence, Presence </div> </div> </div>Rather than combine clans, I'd rather add a fourth discipline to heighten the already existing character of the clans. The issue is... I think 3 disciplines are really the perfect amount for each clan, but for fun we can try: <br /> <br /> Bru Cel, Pot, Pre. Val<br /> Gan: Ani,Cel, For, Prot, <br /> Mal: Aus, Dom, Obf, <b>Obten, </b><br /> Nos: Ani, Obf, Pot, <b>Pro or Nec (Argue about it)</b><br /> Tor: Aus,Cel,Pres, <b>Chi</b><br /> Tre: aus, Dom, Tha... erm... drawing a blank here. Obf would make em too much like the malks... Diomonion? Countermagic? Flight? Sanguinis? <br /> Ven: <b>Aus</b>, Dom,For, Pre<br /> <br /> If we want to include the other clans. <br /> <br /> AsS: Ani<br /> AsV Pre<br /> AsW Pot<br /> Baa Aus<br /> FoS: Tha<br /> FoS(w): Obf<br /> Gio: Aus<br /> Las: Obf... eh maybe that'd mitigate the weakness too much. Aus? Pres?<br /> Rav: Aus<br /> Tzi: For<br /> <br /> Challenge me on anything. Explaining is fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T06:54:27-07:00","id":1461950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461942#post1461942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rather than combine clans, I'd rather add a fourth discipline to heighten the already existing character of the clans. The issue is... I think 3 disciplines are really the perfect amount for each clan, but for fun we can try:<br /> <br /> Bru Cel, Pot, Pre. Val<br /> Gan: Ani,Cel, For, Prot,<br /> Mal: Aus, Dom, Obf, <b>Obten, </b><br /> Nos: Ani, Obf, Pot, <b>Pro or Nec (Argue about it)</b><br /> Tor: Aus,Cel,Pres, <b>Chi</b><br /> Tre: aus, Dom, Tha... erm... drawing a blank here. Obf would make em too much like the malks... Diomonion? Countermagic? Flight? Sanguinis?<br /> Ven: <b>Aus</b>, Dom,For, Pre<br /> <br /> If we want to include the other clans.<br /> <br /> AsS: Ani<br /> AsV Pre<br /> AsW Pot<br /> Baa Aus<br /> FoS: Tha<br /> FoS(w): Obf<br /> Gio: Aus<br /> Las: Obf... eh maybe that'd mitigate the weakness too much. Aus? Pres?<br /> Rav: Aus<br /> Tzi: For<br /> <br /> Challenge me on anything. Explaining is fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've thought about adding a 4th Discipline to Clans as well, maybe using that to broaden the archetype a bit. I found that I often either added Auspex or Fortitude and those Disciplines were over-represented and I was hoping to have the Disciplines spread out relatively evenly.<br /> <br /> For example, I could see giving the Nosferatu Auspex, since they are a Clan of spies and information dealers, and Auspex is so helpful for that. Malkavians with the Auspex and Obfuscate combination could be better spies. The Brujah could also gain Auspex to show their philosophical roots, Ventrue because rulers need to be insightful.<br /> <br /> Something I've always though the Malkavians should have is Fortitude. Crazy people are often portrayed as being tough, like the Joker isn't exceptionally strong or fast, but he is virtually immune to pain and takes beatings without dying or getting severely injured. It also improves their survivability too, which is good if you're getting into trouble. I'm curious to learn why Obtenebration is your choice for them. <br /> <br /> I might give the Tremere Animalism. It goes along with wizards having familiars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T07:17:47-07:00","id":1461952,"title":"","content":"I haven't thought very deeply into how this would work overall, but I have the feeling that these guys would create a very unstable vampire society. I couldn't decide on discipline spreads so I just picked one clan-specific discipline and I guess the other two/three are up in the air. Could vary by individual, or vary by in-clan factions (ie, bloodlines) Might use these for Requiem, actually. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Shapeshifters that tend to be the alien/beastial type</b><br /> [Gangrel+Tzimisce]<br /> <i>Protean/Vicissitude</i><br /> - Mutable flesh, the pro is that you can mould yourself and others. The con is that, when you frenzy, your flesh moulds itself without any input and won't change back to its original state and sooner or later you're going to be very visibly inhuman. You get one such mutation at embrace. Some go for an animal vibe, others go for an abstract vibe, some just go for cool body mods.</li> <li><b>Lord of darkness</b><br /> [Lasombra+Ventrue]<br /> <i>Obtenebration</i><br /> - The Abyss eats your reflection and now it lives inside your corpse. I might actually go for the full V5 Lasombra weakness here. Voice doesn't echo, recordings don't pick up any sensory imput from you, image doesn't show on any surfaces... Unable to use tech or hide what they are very well, the easiest way to get by is to either forgo human society altogether and become some kind of eldricht monstrosity or to be the world's worst control freak and delegate.</li> <li><b>Monsters by monster standards</b><br /> [Assamite + Tremere]<br /> <i>Thaumaturgy/Quietus </i>(Mashup shifted to focus on manipulating vitae for tracking and torture, with other blood magic paths added on as secondary)<br /> - Cursed only to be able to feed on vitae, so understandably these guys are a) prefered dead by the others vampires and b) tend to band together for protection. Blood sorcery and organisation makes them preferable on your side than against you, despite the cost, though some of them don't want to be on your side and prefer to take the Banu Haqim &quot;divinely ordained judge, jury, executioner&quot; role.</li> <li><b>Deader than thou</b><br /> [Hecata+Nosferatu]<br /> <i>Necromancy</i><br /> - Painful bite, no blush of life. Tend to be fond of places that have or had ancestor worship, where they tie their mortal descendants to them in cults (large or small). Or they live in hidden communities, Nosferatu Warren style. Creepy cillages of the dead out of view that nobody wants to think about, learning all your secrets. They make great spies and investigators - or zombie rental stores. I quite like the idea of them also using Dominate, Auspex and Obfuscate in a way that mimics wraiths (invisibility, posession, lifesight (auras), memory manipulation, etc).</li> <li>&quot;<b>Protectors&quot; of Humanity</b><br /> [Brujah+Torador+Salubri]<br /> <i>Obeah/Valeren,</i><br /> - The Brujah's emotional instability with the Toreador's pretentious and dangerous obsession with society and culture, topped off with the Salubri &quot;holier than thou&quot; crap. Absolutely no emotional filter. What they like is an obsession. What they own they control to every inch. What pisses them off triggers a frenzy. Clan culture often hyperfocuses on various aspects of society (art, philosophy, politics, history, religion, military, science, w/e), combined with their &quot;medical&quot; capabilities, they tend to see themselves as the &quot;good&quot; vampires. They preserve and nurture culture, partake in human social movements to change society for whatever they consider better, and shepherd their flocks whether the humans want that or not.</li> <li><b>Seers/Mystic/Failed a Sanity check types</b><br /> [Ravnos+Malkavian]<br /> <i>Chimestry,</i><br /> - You get to see the cosmic truth of the universe. A) the Truth is horrifying B) your mortal shaped mind can't comprehend it, so the information is poorly translated, intrusive and traumatic. On the other hand this horrific insight comes with the ability to manipulate the projection of the false world around you. Yay.</li> <li><b>Eviler <i>and</i> Holier than thou</b><br /> [Setite+Baali+Ravnos]<br /> <i>Daimonion,</i><br /> - Ravnos DAV20 weakness tweaked a bit, every one of them has a compulsion. Vice, virtue, folkloric, totally random... Available to interpretation or bizarrely specific. Might be &quot;unable to lie&quot;, &quot;slay at least one adult man every midnight of a new moon&quot;, &quot;don't enter a house without permission&quot;, &quot;if there are grains of rice in front of you, stop and count every one,&quot; etc. That and their insight into the dirty hidden secrets of the world around them has created a clan culture where the party line is &quot;we are divine monsters ordained by [insert higher power here] to shepherd and/or destroy this unclean world.&quot;</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 09-29-2021, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T07:44:03-07:00","id":1461953,"title":"","content":"I think the issue is that most clans are really well done by the 3 disciplines they have, and for a lot of clans.. other disciplines are unsuitable. Like I said Toreador would get Chimistry because they're focused on beauty and they like to live a lie, but a big thing about Toreador for me is how utterly <i>vapid</i> they are. Of the 7 clans, the others are rather specialized, and the Toreador are the one clan that's gone the jack of all trades route, with the weakest weakness. They're a clan with relatively little direction, and giving them something <i>hard</i> like chimestry gives them direction, which runs counter to the attitudes of the clan... Yeah I guess I can refluff chimestry as easy, but I think what out-of clans a Toreador develops is more interesting than what their in-clans are. Having a fourth discipline de-incintivizes distinguishing yourself from the rest of the clan. <br /> <br /> The Tremere are the biggest issue because they have thaumaturgy and <i>none of the common disciplines suit them</i>. . Mechanically, Fortitude works well for them, but Fortitude just isn't their style. Obfuscate also works for them mechanically, but they're the one group of vampire sorcerers that bands together well enough that they don't hide from other vampires. Presence? They're unlikeable. Animalism? Still unlikeable, and doesn't really suit their style like it would other thaumaturges. Potence? They're not brutes. Celerity? You think someone who spends his unlife hunched over books is going to develop that? Fortitude? New money!. Giving a clan two rare disciplines isn't something wise, and countermagic doesn't register to most vampires. The Tremere's three disciplines are just perfect for them and you end up diminishing the character of the clan adding another. <br /> <br /> On the otherhand, Brujah with Valeren? Why not make the Angry clan angrier? <i>perfection. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T09:33:59-07:00","id":1461970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461952#post1461952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't thought very deeply into how this would work overall, but I have the feeling that these guys would create a very unstable vampire society. I couldn't decide on discipline spreads so I just picked one clan-specific discipline and I guess the other two/three are up in the air. Could vary by individual, or vary by in-clan factions (ie, bloodlines) Might use these for Requiem, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool Clan arrangement. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Combining Tremere with Assamites is an interesting choice, I think it really works.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I would give the evil Clan Damoinon, but I'm not that big a fan of that Discipline. Maybe it should be Dark Thaumaturgy. I think that making Necromancy the evil Discipline could be thematic too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461953#post1461953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue is that most clans are really well done by the 3 disciplines they have, and for a lot of clans.. other disciplines are unsuitable. Like I said Toreador would get Chimistry because they're focused on beauty and they like to live a lie, but a big thing about Toreador for me is how utterly <i>vapid</i> they are. Of the 7 clans, the others are rather specialized, and the Toreador are the one clan that's gone the jack of all trades route, with the weakest weakness. They're a clan with relatively little direction, and giving them something <i>hard</i> like chimestry gives them direction, which runs counter to the attitudes of the clan... Yeah I guess I can refluff chimestry as easy, but I think what out-of clans a Toreador develops is more interesting than what their in-clans are. Having a fourth discipline de-incintivizes distinguishing yourself from the rest of the clan.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are the biggest issue because they have thaumaturgy and <i>none of the common disciplines suit them</i>. . Mechanically, Fortitude works well for them, but Fortitude just isn't their style. Obfuscate also works for them mechanically, but they're the one group of vampire sorcerers that bands together well enough that they don't hide from other vampires. Presence? They're unlikeable. Animalism? Still unlikeable, and doesn't really suit their style like it would other thaumaturges. Potence? They're not brutes. Celerity? You think someone who spends his unlife hunched over books is going to develop that? Fortitude? New money!. Giving a clan two rare disciplines isn't something wise, and countermagic doesn't register to most vampires. The Tremere's three disciplines are just perfect for them and you end up diminishing the character of the clan adding another.<br /> <br /> On the otherhand, Brujah with Valeren? Why not make the Angry clan angrier? <i>perfection. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned earlier that I felt inclined to give several Clans Fortitude, and the Toreador are one of them. I first thought about doing that when I decided on giving the Zantosa Revenant family Fortitude, because they are such hedonists that they push their bodies to the limits - drugs, S&amp;M stuff, self mutilation, extreme partying for hours and hours. Fortitude seems appropriate. If the Toreador got Fortitude it could fit with that idea as well, though it would change the flavor of them a little bit. The artistic, poetic, elite &quot;beautiful people&quot; aren't supposed to be tough, they are supposed to be fragile - that is the stereotype and Clans play on stereotypes to a large extent. But if they got Fortitude, they wouldn't just be those effete artists.<br /> <br /> Fortitude maybe fits with the Tremere? Nah, not really, but it fits better than the other physical Disciplines.<br /> <br /> In some cases, a 4th Discipline fits fairly well with an established Clan. In other cases, its hard to imagine a 4th Discipline. I can't really see the Brujah with Valeren, they don't really seem that well suited to a 4th Discipline to me without some kind of Clan recombination or redefining and/or expanding Clan themes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T10:09:19-07:00","id":1461973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461970#post1461970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure if I would give the evil Clan Damoinon, but I'm not that big a fan of that Discipline. Maybe it should be Dark Thaumaturgy. I think that making Necromancy the evil Discipline could be thematic too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I picked it for being one of the &quot;insider-specific&quot; disciplines that focused on preying on people's weaknesses and guilt, but Dark Thaumaturgy works too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461942#post1461942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mal: Aus, Dom, Obf, <b>Obten, </b></div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of like the idea of Malkavians with Obtenebration, but I'm curious as to why you'd give it to them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nos: Ani, Obf, Pot, <b>Pro or Nec (Argue about it)</b> </div> </div> </div>Protean. Samedi are already near enough Nosferatu with Necromancy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tre: aus, Dom, Tha... erm... drawing a blank here. Obf would make em too much like the malks... Diomonion? Countermagic? Flight? Sanguinis? </div> </div> </div>Obeah or Vicissitude, due to side effects of the vitae they created themselves from and Antediluvian fuckery? Most of them would probably never manifest it anyway, not knowing they have it or having a teacher.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we want to include the other clans.<br /> <br /> AsS: Ani<br /> FoS: Tha<br /> Gio: Aus<br /> Las: Obf... eh maybe that'd mitigate the weakness too much. Aus? Pres?<br /> Tzi: For<br /> <br /> Challenge me on anything. Explaining is fun. </div> </div> </div>Curious about the reasoning for these ones. Tzimisce due to fleshcrafting?<br /> I <i>can</i> see the Giovanni with Auspex. They still stick out for being the only necromancers without fortitude, but compared to the other bloodlines they're kinda ghost-themed to everybody else's corpse-theme so it works. Also enables them further control over their family/cult members. How annoying must it be when your parents can read your mind...<br /> I'm tempted to sarcastically suggest giving the Lasombra Necromancy...<br /> I think I would argue that Obtenebration fits the FoS, due to their anti-light stuff and the destruction of the world goals. Fits with the primordial nothingness of the Abyss and its supposed hatred of existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 09-29-2021, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T10:36:05-07:00","id":1461977,"title":"","content":"Because using Obten is nuts, and I think you'd add to the malkavian sense of craziness if they believed the Darkness was watching them. Abyss mysticism also adds into the whole deal of Malks being seers and mystics. <br /> <br /> The Tremere are more Vis than Obeah, but too many hobbies spoils them. I also like the Tremere being.. clean. They're like the Vamp equivolent of a tech company, lots of effort going into research or development of a ritual and then a lot of riding the gravy train. Vicissitude is too laborious for that concept. I think you just pull the clan in a direction it didn't want to head, at least in modern nights. <br /> <br /> I was thinking to give Tzmisce Potence but they're not really aggressive go getters so Fortitude, being a very reserved clan that reacts more than is proactive, works for them. I think these two disciplines would be very good for extreme shape changes. You know, when they do something that's not structurally sound, these two disciplines can take up the slack. I also think it's not a terrible idea to make Tzmisce more comparable to Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T11:20:25-07:00","id":1461983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461942#post1461942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is... I think 3 disciplines are really the perfect amount for each clan</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my first thoughts with the idea of four Disciplines was that individual characters would still only have 3. After some consideration I think it wouldn't affect the Childer, it is more of a personal resonance to the Blood than a Bloodline, so your Childe may have a slightly different spread than yours. So from 4 disciplines you will choose 1 to remain Out-Clan for you, and this choice makes the broader clan have four distinct expressions.<br /> <br /> As for your Tremere, the thought of them having Sanguinus really amuses me. It is weird, but could be a side effect of their specific origin and reinforces the notion of a tight clan. It isn't as if many of them would want to develop the two together anyway. As another option, what about Mytherceria? The two first levels are great perception powers for magicians and don't superimpose that much with Auspex, while the others still do something I can think of the Tremere doing. You just need to reskin the Discipline to sound less fairies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T18:41:11-07:00","id":1462055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461973#post1461973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protean. Samedi are already near enough Nosferatu with Necromancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nosferatu with Necromancy would be basically like Samedi. Maybe that would be interesting though. That would lead us to an entirely new thought exercise: replacing Clans with Bloodlines <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461973#post1461973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obeah or Vicissitude, due to side effects of the vitae they created themselves from and Antediluvian fuckery? Most of them would probably never manifest it anyway, not knowing they have it or having a teacher.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t see the Tremere with Obeah without a significant reimagining of the Clan. Which we can do, it\u2019s a thread for it, but it seems unthematic to me. Maybe Vicissitude. In that case, the Tremere could be the creepy flesh shaping Clan, which also changes the Clan, but it could be cool. Like MWiS, I\u2019m not sure if I want a Clan to have two special Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461973#post1461973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious about the reasoning for these ones. Tzimisce due to fleshcrafting?<br /> I <i>can</i> see the Giovanni with Auspex. They still stick out for being the only necromancers without fortitude, but compared to the other bloodlines they're kinda ghost-themed to everybody else's corpse-theme so it works. Also enables them further control over their family/cult members. How annoying must it be when your parents can read your mind...<br /> I'm tempted to sarcastically suggest giving the Lasombra Necromancy...<br /> I think I would argue that Obtenebration fits the FoS, due to their anti-light stuff and the destruction of the world goals. Fits with the primordial nothingness of the Abyss and its supposed hatred of existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex seems reasonable for the Giovanni, though I don\u2019t too many Clans having that - it makes Obfuscate Clans less effective. Obfuscate seems reasonable for Setites too, then again I could see combining the Setites, Baali, and Lasombra into one Clan with Obtenebration. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461977#post1461977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because using Obten is nuts, and I think you'd add to the malkavian sense of craziness if they believed the Darkness was watching them. Abyss mysticism also adds into the whole deal of Malks being seers and mystics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. You could even take that in a Lovecraftian direction, with those who gaze into the Abyss going mad in addition to gaining mystical insights. I think Obtenebration has a lot of good thematic potential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1461977#post1461977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> was thinking to give Tzmisce Potence but they're not really aggressive go getters so Fortitude, being a very reserved clan that reacts more than is proactive, works for them. I think these two disciplines would be very good for extreme shape changes. You know, when they do something that's not structurally sound, these two disciplines can take up the slack. I also think it's not a terrible idea to make Tzmisce more comparable to Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly see similarities to the Ventrue and Tzimisce. Through out my thoughts of Clan combinations, I have though that there should basically be two leadership Clans, one which is traditional, conservative, yet also honorable while the other should be more ruthless, less traditional and honor bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T07:50:13-07:00","id":1492091,"title":"","content":"Alright, here's another set of recombined Clans along the same lines:<br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce/Nosferatu/Cappadocian: Animalism, Fortitude, Necromancy, Potence</b><br /> Weakness: These vampires are pale and cold, unable to use blush of life. For each night that they go without sleeping surrounded by earth from their homeland, their Appearance is reduced by 1. If their Appearance becomes 0, then they are obviously inhuman, appearing as a decaying corpse. Appearance returns at the rate of one point per day of slumber in their homeland\u2019s soil.<br /> These vampires are lords of death, removed from mortal cities and civilizations, they are feudal lords whose power was at its zenith centuries ago. Now they find themselves removed from the mortal world, still clinging to their ancient estates, served by animals, their ghostly and zombie servants, and old inbred revenant families. They are among the most conservative of Clans.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere/Assamite: Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate, Sorcery</b><br /> Weakness: When they arose in the Middle Ages and began to slay with vampires, they were hunted nearly to extinction and only avoided it by accepting a necromantic curse \u2013 taking an unsoakable aggravated wound for every point of vampire blood that they consume.<br /> A mortal group of mystical assassins and vampire hunters who sought to use stolen vampire blood to gain immortality. Later they usurped another Clan to gain full Clan status. They now offer their services to other Clans \u2013 as wizards, spies, or assassins.<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue/Malkavian: Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate, Presence</b><br /> Weakness: All vampires of this Clan have a single derangement, usually related to megalomania, narcissism, or something else related to craving power or pridefulness.<br /> This is a Clan of master manipulators. They crave power and prestige, they want to be loved, admired, to have the power of influencing others\u2019 hearts and minds. They are known to be masters of manipulation, whether through magical means or mundane, and are the vampires with the greatest amount of temporal wealth and power.<br /> <br /> <b>Toreador/Lasombra: Celerity, Obtenebration, Potence, Presence</b><br /> Weakness: Cursed to cast no reflection, members of this Clan are obsessed with their own image and may be captivated by painting or other likenesses of themselves.<br /> These vampires are lords and ladies of the night. They are passionate, love beauty and death and darkness. The see themselves are royalty of sorts, fit to rule, to be pampered and pleasured by servants. In the modern era, many take up gothic styles, wearing black or even symbols of darkness or evil.<br /> <br /> <b>Setite/Giovanni: Dominate, Necromancy, Obfuscate, Potence</b><br /> Weakness: As the Giovanni weakness<br /> An ancient inbred family from Egypt, who claim to trace their ancestry to the pharaohs and priests of ancient Egypt, they are a mortal family as much as a vampire Clan. They practice an ancient form of Egyptian necromancy and still worship the gods of Egypt and incorporate that religion into their magic. Not only do they pursue the mystical arts, but also dedicate themselves to acquiring wealth and power, using their mental powers and family connections to create a web of influence across the world. Most members of the Clan draw upon the family and so are of old Egyptian ancestry.<br /> <br /> <b>Salubri/Brujah: Auspex, Celerity, Dominate, Fortitude</b><br /> Weakness: When members of this Clan drink blood from an unwilling human, they must make a frenzy roll with a difficulty of 5 + number of blood points consumed. Even if they resist this frenzy, drinking blood from the unwilling increases rolls to resist frenzy by 1 for one day per point consumed.<br /> This is a Clan of philosophers and even humanitarians. They have long hoped to overcome the weaknesses of the vampire state, pursuing legend of Golconda. They have also long been rebels, seeing the oppressive nature of power structures and supporting Anarchs and other movements that resist oppression by the elders. They also strive to protect humans from exploitation by vampires. While some of these vampires settle into a single city, forming the backbone of Anarch movements, others prefer a nomadic existence to avoid corrupt vampiric politics.<br /> <br /> <b>Baali/Gangrel: Animalism, Fortitude, Presence, Protean</b><br /> Weakness: Vampires of this Clan suffer more from True Faith than other vampires. Any human with a Humanity of 6 or higher counts as having +1 point of True Faith against these vampires, which means that even people without True Faith can harm or repel these vampires by brandishing symbols of goodness. Furthermore, when vampires of this Clan frenzy, they take on a bestial animal-like appearance that could violate the Masquerade.<br /> This is a Clan of witches, living deep in the woods away from humanity, sometimes surrounded by human cults or servants, they may be the origin of many myths of witchcraft. Many of these vampires worship demons or pagan gods of evil, some even practice sorcery or receive demonic gifts from their dark rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T10:24:23-07:00","id":1492099,"title":"","content":"With just thinking about it on the fly here would be my tentative list:<br /> <br /> (Assamite + Brujah): Warrior Philosophers and judges of men's worth. They burn with the love of ideologies and harshly judge those that would seek to do injustice against those same ideas. <br /> <br /> (Gangrel + Nosferatu): The Clan of monster, of animals, of the wild. This clan is what does bump in the night, what lurks in the dark forest, what stalks you on the road when you are by yourself.<br /> <br /> (Followers of Set + Toreador): Clan of mystics and hedonist, they love the creation of passions even if that passion drives people into darkness. Rejecters of the sin of flesh and embracers of the purity of the unbridled energy of passion.<br /> <br /> (Giovanni + Lasombra + Ventrue): The strong arm, the suits, lord and ladies of the high castle. They don't just run the show, they <b>are</b> the show. They own it, grown it, blown it, and can buy you over and over.<br /> <br /> (Tremere + Tzimisce): Sorcerers, Wizards, Welders of will. The strange clan that uses the power of their blood to impose upon the universe and steal form the abyss of all knowledge. But magic is a gate way to power that some might call unnatural.<br /> <br /> (Malkavian + Ravnos): Oracles and Priest, their blood allows them to see the truth of the world and manipulate it but, at a price. Strange to those unfamiliar but, a valuable companion in a world filled with illusions.<br /> <br /> (Catiff/Wildcard): Pariah and outcast. Untrusted by most, these clanless are unpredictable. Most seek to either chase the clanless out of their cities are make them useful tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T23:25:11-07:00","id":1492137,"title":"","content":"My version:<br /> <br /> Bru: Cel, Pot, Pre, Pro<br /> Gan: Ani, For, Obf, Pro<br /> Mal: Aus, Dom, Obf, Chi<br /> Nos: Ani, Cel, Obf, Pot<br /> Tor: Aus, Cel, Pre, Chi<br /> Tre: Ani, Aus, Dom, For<br /> Ven: Dom, For, Pot, Pre<br /> <br /> Total: Ani 3, Aus 3, Cel 3, Chi 2, Dom 3, For 3, Obf 3, Pot 3, Pre 3, Pro 2<br /> <br /> Although, I think a more interesting version of this game would be to do the Hecata thing and blend VTM clans according to the alliances they'd make for survival.<br /> <br /> So, assume all the clans' founders have woken up, slaked their Hunger on their grandchilder, and left all the clans fragmented and broken (and the sects are shattered too). How would they reconstitute themselves to survive?<br /> <br /> I could see it going along Second Generation lines, for example. Or along the lines of which Disciplines they favour.<br /> <br /> So the Hecata is a given. I'll give them Dominate, Fortitude, Potence. Necromancy is available to them at out of clan costs.<br /> <br /> Let's say the FoS+Baali+Lasombra become a new clan, Obsidia, that controls mortal religions from the shadows and acts as priests to vampire-kind. Weakness: No reflection, double damage from sunlight and True Faith. Disciplines: Dominate, Obfuscate, Presence. Obtenebration is available out of clan.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Assamites+Tremere+Tzimisce, becoming a new sorcerer clan, Ashipu. They are scholars, lords and occultists, often living in remote places but commanding mortal cults to serve them. Weakness: Being away from their home turf weakens them, as per the Tzimisce weakness. They cannot make blood bonds and their vitae is mutagenic to other vampires. Disciplines: Animalism, Auspex, Protean. Thaumaturgy is out of clan.<br /> <br /> Brujah+Toreador+Ravnos+Malkavian become the decadent ravers, the Istarri. Driven by intense passions, they are driven by vice and indulgence. Weakness: +2 difficulty to resist indulging a vice. All gain a single obsession in addition to this. Disciplines: Auspex, Obfuscate, Presence. Chimerstry is out of clan for them.<br /> <br /> Gangrel+Nosferatu become the Neferat, a clan of monsters who take on the blighted forms of the places they inhabit. Weakness: Neferat distort the places they are in. Sewers are filled with mutant rats and become mazelike tunnels that trap prey. A forest becomes a nightmare place of darkness and savage animals. The Neferat changes in turn, taking on monstrous features in alignment with their domain. In addition, their social pools are capped by their Humanity, due to this level of monstrosity. (They ignore this penalty when dealing with allies.) Disciplines: Animalism, Obfuscate, Protean. Maybe they can take Sanguinis out of clan, which in this case would allow them to swap body parts and merge with the animals/critters in their domain. It might have some elements of Visceratika woven into it.<br /> <br /> Ventrue+DoC+Salubri become the Baobani, a clan of leaders and prophets whose siren song allows them to calm the kine, seduce Kindred and heal the sick. Weakness: They cannot feed from the unwilling, though they can use their siren call to bewitch their marks. Disciplines: Auspex, Dominate, Presence. Obeah would be out of clan and Melpominee would be folded into Presence. Obeah would work via song instead of touch.<br /> <br /> Totals: Animalism 2, Auspex 3, Dominate 3, Fortitude 1, Obfuscate 3, Potence 1, Presence 3, Protean 2. I could shift things around a bit more for a more even spread, but I don't mind this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 09-02-2022, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T05:08:34-07:00","id":1492153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1492137#post1492137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My version:Totals: Animalism 2, Auspex 3, Dominate 3, Fortitude 1, Obfuscate 3, Potence 1, Presence 3, Protean 2. I could shift things around a bit more for a more even spread, but I don't mind this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't help but notice the only of your new groupings that have physical attributes are the Hecata. You could give them Auspex, Dominate, and Necromancy - then you could make physical attributes equal across the board.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T11:39:54-07:00","id":1492178,"title":"","content":"Here is my attempt at this post.<br /> <br /> Followers Of Set &amp; Tremere: The outcasts of Kindred society who seek out dark and dangerous lore and practice potent and dangerous blood magics in the name of Set and other blood Gods. Yet many Kindred feel the need to make deals with them as there information gathering network and diveristy of contacts is superior to even the Nosferatu can even muster at any given time and a willing to grant with no seeming strings attached.<br /> <br /> Disciplines Spread: Auspex, Blood Sorcery, Potence and Presence.<br /> <br /> Weakness: I would keep the original weakness and maybe the Assamite Sorceror caste weakness of being unable to conceal there mystic nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T10:12:31-07:00","id":1492234,"title":"","content":"Another combo I had thought of is Banu Haqim/Ventrue: The self proclaimed rulers and judges of kindred society who feel a need to guide the other lesser clans by example and judge others by there incredibly high standards and dispose of those who are unworthy of the blood and try to curb the worst excesses of there kind as they know that humanity can wipe them out by sheer numbers and advanced weapons.<br /> <br /> Discipline spread: Auspex, Dominate Fortitude &amp; Presence:<br /> <br /> Weakness: They must feed from a specfic group of humans to avoid hunger frenzies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T01:16:19-07:00","id":1492266,"title":"","content":"Were I to do this... <br /> <br /> I'd just use the Main 7 clans. Or 6+caitiff<br /> Wait I really like the Potence/Dominate and Obfuscate Presence combination... <br /> Alright: <br /> <br /> Brujah, Gangrel, Malkavian, Nosferatu, Toreador and Ventrue stay as they are. What's interesting would be how the other clans/disciplines are handled. <br /> <br /> Tremere are Caitiff<br /> Assamites, FoS, Ravnos are cults not clans. <br /> The <b>Lasombra</b> and Tzmisce are clubs other clans can join (mostly Malkavians) (Note: Lasombra is a much less stupid name when it's a club you can join rather than a clan)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The old Clan specific Disciplines still exist, they just have side effects for learning. This is why you're probably going to join a cult/sect once you learn them</b>. Exotic bloods are highly beneficial for these disciplines, but these too come with side effects. <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy, Protean and Necromancy just have a lot of social baggage around them. They're not faction specific and don't need exotic blood: every vampire is capable of discovering these powers on their own provided they have the knowledge. This includes Variants of these powers like Serpentis, Thanatosis, Akhu, Dur-An-Ki and so on. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Chimestry</b><br /> Chimestry can be developed from the blood of changelings, or those who teach the discipline. More than the blood, the power requires a certain level of philosophical and cognitive alteration: The practitioner must believe in their own illusions while simultaneously not believing in them enough that they don't accidentally break them. Chimestry burns through a lot of willpower so it doesn't per-se need a massive adjustment for a weakness. Perhaps, after each use, the user becomes weak to cold iron for a time. Cold iron doing aggravated damage. Hunting Changelings is also quite dangerous. Perhaps users might also be more susceptible to flights of fancy/vice/derangements while they have changeling blood within them. <br /> <br /> <b>Diamonion</b><br /> Learned through the blood of demons or those contaminated. Having such blood within you will cause paranormal phenomena and practicing the discipline will increase the user's vulnerability to faith. <br /> <br /> <b>Obtenebration:</b> <br /> The blood of the monsters who originated this power are exceedingly rare and so this power is usually taught to those who can pass the cruel trials of the Lasombra. Every single power has a side effect when used that persists for a time after use. Usually an anti-social supernatural effect; something like eerie presence or losing your reflection. The higher level the power, the bigger the issue. <br /> <br /> <b>Quietus: </b><br /> Learned by drinking from poisoned/drugged individuals. Vampires have their skin darken according to how many levels of Quietus they have. This darkening is similar to that of Arsenic poisoning. Using my Quietus book, the first level of quietus allows the vampire to safely store a poison/drug in their body for later use, one point per level of Quietus. This is not terribly uncommon and the darkening effect is barely apparent at first level. However later levels require delving further into sampling poisoned/drugged blood and can take quite a toll on the user's humanity. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Vicissitude</b><br /> Drinking from fleshcrafted creatures provides the blood needed for vicissitude. Vicissitude is somewhat addicting and many will self destruct looking for metamorphosis, kinda like a bodybuilder ruining his body in the pursuit of looking more than healthy. However, the true costs of vicissitude come from it's experiments: A shaper will need a lot of practice and that comes at the lives of hundreds of test subjects (hopefully animals) which has a huge impact on anyone on the path of humanity. Many Elders also persecute shapers: The ability to grant wanted criminals new faces to hide behind is a strong destabilizer for polite kindred society. Some versions of the book of Nod also condemn the practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T04:36:11-07:00","id":1492288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1492266#post1492266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Note: Lasombra is a much less stupid name when it's a club you can join rather than a clan)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to nitpick just one part of your otherwise cool post, but why is Lasombra a stupid name? Univerbation is a common feature of many Romance languages. We have examples of real-world surnames like the French Legrand, which, if &quot;translated,&quot; would be &quot;Thegreat,&quot; or the Spanish Laguardia, &quot;Theguard,&quot; or the Italian &quot;Laporta,&quot; &quot;Thedoor.&quot; But nobody ever &quot;translates&quot; real-world family names in an attempt to show how dumb they are. It's only fictional names that are ever stupid, or illogical, or any other bunch of complaints I've seen over the years. I've never really understood why voicing concerns over fictional names is so common among roleplaying fans in particular. Real-world names are often dumb as shit, too.<br /> <br /> Just about the only complaint concerning the names of the vampire clans that I think is valid is that the clans are supposed to predate the languages from which they take their names by millennia. However, that is only a problem if you ascribe to the idea that vampiric society is completely static and no linguistic drift whatsoever takes place over the course of centuries. I think the lexicon sections common to all White Wolf game lines demonstrate that that's untrue. Personally, I don't think that <i>any</i> of the current clan names are older than 500 years, with a few exceptions (such as, appropriately enough, Clan Tzimisces). My view is that whenever <i>Dark Ages</i> books and other material set in the distant past use the modern clan names, it's simply a convenience for the sake of the reader. After all, the characters in the books also speak and write in modern English, not Medieval Latin or whatever, for reasons that are just as obvious.<br /> <br /> Anyway, rant over. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T05:05:54-07:00","id":1492291,"title":"","content":"Brujah meaning &quot;Witch&quot; is good dumb fun and I think the rebelious Brujah would mostly be very happy with it. <br /> But &quot;The Shadow&quot; is decisively uncool. Granted, the Lasombra are very often caught up in their Ch\u016bniby\u014d phase but... would the name really be decided upon by <i>them? </i>IDK about you but I'd think most Lasombra are too elitist to pick such a base name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T08:14:11-07:00","id":1492297,"title":"","content":"Well, to elaborate on the view I expressed above about the modern clan names being no more than 500 years old, I also don't think that any of the clan names were decided upon by the clan members themselves. Ventrue would not have proudly called themselves &quot;potbellied.&quot; Nosferatu <i>might</i> have purposefully taken on the name &quot;disease-bearers&quot; with grins on their ugly faces, but most likely it was just another nickname that eventually became the &quot;real&quot; clan name through linguistic drift. Similarly, I think Lasombra just got called &quot;the shadows&quot; by others for long enough that eventually it stuck. The nicknames of today, like &quot;blue bloods,&quot; &quot;sewer rats,&quot; and &quot;keepers,&quot; might be the &quot;proper&quot; clan names of the distant future (assuming there is no Gehenna to end it all in the interim).<br /> <br /> I'm also not convinced that Brujah was ever meant to be a Spanish word. I will grant you that it has been a popular thing to say among the fandom for 30 years, but I've never seen or heard Rein-Hagen confirm it. Spanish words don't end in <i>h,</i> but it's a common feature in other languages, and as it happens, <i>brujah</i> (<b><i>with</i></b> an <i>h</i>) is a legitimate word in <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brujati\" target=\"_blank\">several Slavic languages</a>. <i>\u0411\u0440\u0443\u0301\u0458\u0430\u0442\u0438</i> is an onomatopoeic expression that means to drone, hum, sizzle, or hiss. <i>\u0411\u0440\u0443\u0458\u0430\u0445 (brujah)</i> is simply the past tense of the verb.<br /> <br /> I make no claims that this is the &quot;real&quot; definition of Clan Brujah, but I have just as much evidence for this being the case as the people who insist that Brujah means &quot;witch with an <i>h</i> stuck at the end&quot; have for theirs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 09-04-2022, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T08:48:48-07:00","id":1492301,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:31px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Yeah I wans't convinced of the &quot;witch&quot; thing either. It just seemed a point people liked to bring up here</span><br /> <br /> brou\u00b7haha</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">[\u02c8bru\u02d0h\u0251\u02d0h\u0251\u02d0] </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">NOUN</span></span></span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#111111\"><b>a noisy and overexcited reaction or response to something:</b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#767676\">&quot;the brouhaha over those infamous commercials&quot; \u00b7 </span></b> <b><span style=\"color:#767676\">[More]</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#767676\"><b><i>synonyms:</i></b><br /> <b>disturbance \u00b7 racket \u00b7 uproar \u00b7 tumult \u00b7 ruckus \u00b7 clamour \u00b7 furore \u00b7 hue and cry \u00b7 palaver \u00b7 fuss \u00b7 stir \u00b7 to-do \u00b7 storm \u00b7 maelstrom \u00b7 melee \u00b7 turmoil \u00b7 disorder \u00b7 confusion \u00b7 chaos \u00b7 mayhem \u00b7 havoc \u00b7 pandemonium \u00b7 upheaval \u00b7 unrest \u00b7 fracas \u00b7 riot \u00b7 </b> <b>[More]</b></span></span></span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T10:00:32-07:00","id":1492308,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm aware of the <i>brouhaha</i> suggestion, but I don't think it's any more convincing than Spanish witches. The pronunciation guide for Brujah on page 136 of the original 1991 core book is <i>&quot;br\u014d\u014d' j\u00e4&quot;</i>, which doesn't resemble any real-world word I know of. However, since the pronunciation guide is for English speakers, the <i>j</i> would be pronounced like the one in <i>jaw,</i> I think. There's no way an English speaker would come up with <i>\u02c8bru\u02d0h\u0251\u02d0</i> from <i>br\u014d\u014d' j\u00e4</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T14:54:05-07:00","id":1492319,"title":"","content":"A few years ago I saw an interview with Mark Rein-Hagen and he pronounced the \u201cj\u201d in Brujah in the English way, not like a Spanish h sound. Which suggests to me that he never intended their name to sound like the Spanish word for witch and that the similar spelling is just a coincidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T21:35:00-07:00","id":1492340,"title":"","content":"English is in the minority for using J like dg. Only french is a little similar. Almost everyone else in europe uses it like a y. <br /> <br /> Still, even the dg way to say Brujah doesn't sound too far off Brouhaha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T04:25:55-07:00","id":1492356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1492340#post1492340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">English is in the minority for using J like dg. Only french is a little similar. Almost everyone else in europe uses it like a y.<br /> <br /> Still, even the dg way to say Brujah doesn't sound too far off Brouhaha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Portuguese does the same, and maybe Galician. Not quite a dg, but more similar to it than y or h.<br /> <br /> But then, none of those pronunciations get far enough from each other to not ring some bells, and the Spanish <i>Bruja </i>(<i>Broo-ha</i>)is <i>Bruxa</i> in Portuguese (<i>Broo-sha</i>), which sounds even more similar to the dg pronunciation.<br /> <br /> Yet there's a twist to it: this pronunciation with an sh-sounding X <i>also</i> relates to a romance word for &quot;grinding teeth&quot;, still used in Italian with the <i>bruxa</i> inflection (and still present <i>bruxismo</i> in Portuguese, a name for the compulsive grinding of teeth).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T06:19:43-07:00","id":1492426,"title":"","content":"Obviously we need to use the best version of Clan Names, the ones in the Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> No more Ventrue you have Kingship Clan, no more Gangrel you have the Clan of the Beast, no more Malkavian you have the Moon Clan, ect. I think the Lasombra would be either the Clan of the Night or the Night Clan. Brujah would be the Clan of the Learned or the Learned Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T08:42:02-07:00","id":1492432,"title":"","content":"I really have a hard time believing that Brujah were ever scholars when they're geared towards Potence/ Celerity/ Presence. Might be something they did in spite of their tallents/ to focus their rage/so that they have better arguments; but there's nothing about them that suggests they would be more scholarly than any other clan. Venture have as much need of education as Brujah. Maybe it's because it's so surprising that people remember such a thing. Kinda like how dangerous driving isn't newsworthy but a bicycle crash causes folks to lose their mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T09:45:32-07:00","id":1492434,"title":"","content":"Snark aside, Brujah being the 'Learned Clan' falls more into the noddist mythos of the Brujah Antediluvian building the first library in the first city rather then anything with their discipline set or their modern depiction. Just like the Ventrue are not anymore kingly then any other clan in particular.<br /> <br /> The Noddist clan names really play into the idea that each of the Antediluvians had the one thing they did and got their epitaph from. Haqim the Hunter(Judge), Saulot the Healer, Ventru the King(ruler), etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T11:31:42-07:00","id":1492440,"title":"","content":"Quick try, just made it now, just for fun:<br /> (In this world, all Clans have 3 Disciplines (signature ones are <b>bold</b>). Additionally, each Character must choose a 4th Physical one to treat personally as &quot;in-Clan&quot;). For those that want to use specific things of current lore, like Salubri's 3rd eye, just create Bloodlines/Loresheets such as &quot;descendant of Saulot&quot; and assume Antediluvians are &quot;disputed&quot; (no one knows if Absimilliard or Malkav is the &quot;true&quot; Antediluvian of the Cursed).<ul><li><b>The Clan of Rulers (Ventrue, Lasombra, Banu Haqim)</b><ul><li>These vampires believe they are meant to rule the world with an iron fist, to make the laws and enforce them over anything that &quot;lives&quot;: kindred, men, and beasts alike.<ul><li>Bane: Grounded (same as V5 Tzimisce)</li> <li>Compulsion: Arrogance (same as V5 Ventrue)</li> <li>Disciplines: <b>Dominate</b>, <b>Presence</b>, Animalism. (Most common Physical: Fortitude).</li> </ul></li> <li>&quot;We are the Kings and Judges of Mortals and Immortals alike; our word is the law and you shall obey&quot;.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>The Clan of Shepherds (Toreador, Brujah, Ravnos)</b><ul><li>The Rulers want to live above humans; the Shepherds want to live among them, side by side. Some prefer to mingle with the rich, others with the poor, others with nomads and other with artists, and some simply try to maintain their own normal &quot;lives&quot; among their own people (or the closest to it that they can get).<ul><li>Bane: Feeding Preference (same as V5 Ventrue)</li> <li>Compulsion: Affective Empathy (same as V5 Salubri)</li> <li>Disciplines: <b>Presence</b>, <b>Auspex</b>, Obfuscate. (Most common Physical: Celerity).</li> </ul></li> <li>&quot;Kindred are meant to live side by side with humans, for good or ill, we are two sides of the same ccin.&quot;</li> </ul></li> <li><b>The Clan of Magic (Tremere, Hecata)</b><ul><li>The Vitae is magic, but this Clan's Vitae is even more than most. They &quot;live&quot; to learn all kinds of things, and to study and refine the magic in their blood.<ul><li>Bane: same as V5 Lasombra (problems with mirrors and high technology)</li> <li>Compulsion: Cryptophilia (same as V5 Nosferatu, but many times it becomes a &quot;hunt-for-magic-secrets&quot;)</li> <li>Disciplines: <b>Blood Sorcery</b>, <b>Oblivion</b>, &quot;Thin-Blood&quot; <b>Alchemy</b> (in this world, it works with non-Thinblood Vitae, so its called just &quot;Alchemy&quot;. Common counterfeits are Auspex, Dominate, and Obfuscate/Chimestry). (Most common Physical: Fortitude (including <b><i>Obeah</i></b>)).</li> </ul></li> <li>&quot;I know much, and what I don't yet know, I shall discover soon.&quot;</li> </ul></li> <li><b>The Clan of the Devoted (Salubri, Baali, Ministry)</b><ul><li>Some people think they know what is the right path to follow; these kindred KNOW what they must adhere to. Many are religious or follow some kind of strict behavior code; some follow an old religion (or a kindred-exclusive one), some follow the path to Golconda, some follow infernal tenets or a mission to &quot;corrupt souls&quot;, some enforce a personal code of &quot;right and wrong&quot;, but all of them are very rigid in what they believe, and feel their Blood compelling them to do &quot;what must be done&quot; and to &quot;guide other souls&quot; or even found their own Blood Cult.<ul><li>Bane: fundamentalist people are easy to enrage when confronted. Same as V5 Brujah.</li> <li>Compulsion: Judgement (same as V5 Banu Haqim)</li> <li>Disciplines: <b>Presence</b>, Dominate (note to &quot;Obeah&quot; lvl 5), Auspex. (Most common Physical: Potence).</li> </ul></li> <li>&quot;Are you lost? Let me show you the right path.&quot;</li> </ul></li> <li><b>The Clan of the Cursed (Malkavian, Nosferatu)</b><ul><li>These vampires are the proof that cainites are cursed; the Embrace inevitably distorts them forever. Some carry their curse on their flesh; others, on their mind.<ul><li>Bane: Cursed Flesh (same as Nosferatu) or Cursed Mind (same as Malkavian)</li> <li>Compulsion: Feral Impulses (same as V5 Gangrel) for the Flesh-Cursed, and Delusion (same as V5 Malkavian) for the Mind-Cursed.</li> <li>Disciplines: <b>Auspex</b>, <b>Obfuscate </b>(includes <b><i>Chimestry</i></b>, for &quot;bleeding&quot; their Madness to the world, or to bring nightmares to life), Protean (they see it as the mark of the cursed, since it is clearly supernatural). (Most common Physical: Potence; madmen and monsters are commonly pretty strong and uncontrollable).</li> </ul></li> <li>&quot;Don't be fooled, we kindred are all damned, my curse is just easier to spot than yours.&quot;</li> </ul></li> <li><b>The Clan of Metamorphosis (Gangrel, Tzimisce)</b><ul><li>These vampires accept that they are not human anymore, and embrace their journey to accept themselves as they are or even to become something else. Some get inspirations on animals and their own bestial urges; others, in alien or mystic concepts of transcendence.<ul><li>Bane: same as V5 Gangrel, but not limited to animal-themed: these can be &quot;monster themed&quot; or &quot;cronenberg themed&quot;, based on the character daily actions and beliefs.</li> <li>Compulsion: Transgresssion (same as V5 Ministry), as an urge to &quot;transcend&quot; - or to force others to &quot;transcend&quot; - their 'human' shackles.</li> <li>Disciplines: V5 <b>Protean </b>(includes <b>Vicissitude </b>and <b>One-With-The-Land</b>), Animalism, Dominate (includes <b>Vicissitude</b>). (Most common Physical: Celerity).</li> </ul></li> <li>&quot;I'm more than man or animal; more than alive or dead - I'm something else.&quot;</li> </ul></li> </ul>I'm surprised that i just needed 6 Clans o.O<br /> <br /> hope you all like it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T08:38:34-07:00","id":1492602,"title":"","content":"Personally I use the requiem aproach of 5 clans + bloodlines converting most of the other clans to bloodlines<br /> <br /> For example in my games the LaSombra are a bloodline of the Ventrue born in ancient Rome. However they proclaim not to be a bloodline but the original clan who fell in prestige after the original founder was diabolized by the Ventrue in what was effectively the original anarch revolt. The reason for said revolution was that they where using Obtenebration for dealing with otherwordly beings. The LaSombra criticize the ventrue because their lack of ruthleness was the reason why Carthago became a treat (the eldricth beings allied with the brujah) and later Rome fell. One of LaSombra aspiration was finding Ventrue resting place and diabolice it to make the clan great again.<br /> <br /> <b>Discipline spread: </b>Dominate, Animalism, Obtenebration, Vigor.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Weakness:</b> The LaSombra suffer agravated damage from silver and cannot see their reflection on silver mirrors. Also their deals in the past with eldritch beings make them have a penalty of -1 in all rolls against spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T13:08:38-07:00","id":1492771,"title":"","content":"Here is another possibility inspired by an earlier reply. For these Clans, they have no physical Disciplines, rather all vampires begin with one point of each physical Discipline and can buy them as in Clan Disciplines. Then each Clan has three Clan Disciplines, one of which is a Discipline unique to that Clan.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ventrue/Assamite: Dominate, Quietus, Presence</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: They only get full nourishment from the blood of one kind of vessel, much like the Ventrue weakness, but still get half nourishment from other sources. Furthermore, they cannot drink the blood of other vampires, and will vomit it up if they attempt to do so.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Ventrue are the ancient nobility of the undead. Not only kings, but knights and judges. They are honor bound and traditional, seeking to keep the laws of the Cainite race. They are the Clan most likely to be princes, as well as sheriffs or scourges. The greatest of crimes against the Cainites race is that of diablerie and their revulsion to it is so strong that they cannot even consume the blood of other cainites. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Tremere/Malkavian: Auspex, Dominate, Thaumaturgy</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: Insanity, as Malkavians</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">An order of human wizards who used their magic to transform themselves into vampires. Unfortunately, their magic and the dark secrets they have learned twists the mind, and all have some form of insanity. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Nosferatu/Ravnos: Animalism, Chimerstry, Obfuscate</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: as Nosferatu</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hideously ugly vampires, this Clan either hides within sewers or abandoned building, away from the prying eyes of humans, or the travel from place to place as nomads. Many use their skills to become spies or information brokers, some are even assassins or thieves. They are much like the Nosferatu of canon.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Toreador/Lasombra: Auspex, Obtenebration, Presence</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: As the Lasombra, they have no reflection in mirrors and cannot be captured on film. They are also captivated by images of themselves, such as paintings or sculpture. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dark lord and ladies of the night, this ruthless Clan of darkness sees themselves as fit to rule others. They are also passionate and beautiful, hedonistic, and peruse sadistic pleasures as well as mundane ones. They are most attracted to works of art that reflect dark or macabre aspects of existence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Salubri/Brujah/Setite: Obeah, Obfuscate, Presence </b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: When they drink the blood of unwilling vessels, they must make a hunger frenzy check with a difficulty of 4 + 1 per blood point consumed. Furthermore, drinking the blood of unwilling vessels increases all difficulties to resist frenzies by 1 for the rest of the night. This effect is cumulative for multiple unwilling vessels. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This is a Clan of scholars, rebels, and non-conformists. Many have traditionally upheld more humane or compassionate values - that vampires should show mercy to humans, avoid murder or enslavement of them, even that you vampires should have rights that cannot be violated by the elders. Others reject rules and structures entirely, preferring absolute freedom. Members of this Clan form the backbone of the Anarch movement.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Baali/Giovanni/Cappadocian: Dominate, Necromancy, Obfuscate</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: These vampires are cold and pale, unable to use blush of health. Furthermore, any mortal with a Humanity of 6 or higher counts as having +1 point of True Faith when attempting to combat these vampires with religious items. This can effectively give a humane mortal a True Faith value when they had none previously.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This Clan of vampires serve demonic masters and practice dark magic that allows them to command the souls of the dead or even the forces of death itself. The center of the Clan is an ancient inbred family of demon worships who pass the curse of vampirism through their family, though others exist outside of the family as well. In addition to practicing dark magic, they also peruse wealth and temporal power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Gangrel/Tzimisce: Animalism, Auspex, Protean</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: these vampires must sleep surrounded by or within their native soil. If they do not do so, they gain an animal feature. Each animal feature reduces a single social attribute by 1 point and this is cumulative. If Appearance is reduced to zero this way, then the vampires becomes an obviously inhuman monster. Each night of sleeping with the soil removes one animalistic feature. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This Clan are masters of the wild places and tied to the land itself. Some merely travel across the land preying on animals and living at me with nature. Others lay claim to a domain and rule it, and it\u2019s inhabitants, as masters. The elders of this Clan are extremely traditional and territorial, emphasizing the rule of the elder over his domain.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T14:18:24-07:00","id":1493184,"title":"","content":"Another combo that is swimming around in my brain.<br /> <br /> Brujah/Gangrel: The Monsters: These Kindred are the savage monsters and slippery rebels of vampire society whom seek to tear down the foundations of the vampire ruling class. They can be savage berserkers or subtle infiltrators who worm there way into the power structure and learn the weak points and exploit it.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Celerity, Potence, Presence &amp; Protean.<br /> <br /> Weakness: The Monsters are more prone to frenzies and are at -3 to resist them and after multiple frenzies gain animalistic features subject to the storyteller's discretion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-19-2022, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T22:14:18-07:00","id":1493228,"title":"","content":"This seems like a really fun form of homebrew to try, and I've been toying with the notion of seven clans that reflect the seven houses of the Fallen, drawing inspiration from Buffy the Vampire Slayer's notion of vamps as demon-possessed to smoosh the two splats together.<br /> <br /> I'll give it some more thought and post my ideas. This thread is terrific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T16:06:25-07:00","id":1493604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1493228#post1493228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like a really fun form of homebrew to try, and I've been toying with the notion of seven clans that reflect the seven houses of the Fallen, drawing inspiration from Buffy the Vampire Slayer's notion of vamps as demon-possessed to smoosh the two splats together.<br /> <br /> I'll give it some more thought and post my ideas. This thread is terrific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! You should post your houses of Fallen Clans, I would be interested in seeing that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1493184#post1493184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another combo that is swimming around in my brain.<br /> <br /> Brujah/Gangrel: The Monsters: These Kindred are the savage monsters and slippery rebels of vampire society whom seek to tear down the foundations of the vampire ruling class. They can be savage berserkers or subtle infiltrators who worm there way into the power structure and learn the weak points and exploit it.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Celerity, Potence, Presence &amp; Protean.<br /> <br /> Weakness: The Monsters are more prone to frenzies and are at -3 to resist them and after multiple frenzies gain animalistic features subject to the storyteller's discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, combing both of the anti-authority Clans. I think I would reduce the penalty to resist frenzies to -1 instead, since they have the Gangrel animal feature weakness too. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, here are a few more combination Clans. Once again I gave each Clan a signature Discipline and no physical Disciplines, those will be universal.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ventrue</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ventrue/Lasombra: Dominate, Obtenebration, Presence</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: they have a strong preference for the vitae of a certain kind of vessel (virgins, old men, only animals, etc.) and any other kind of blood only provides 1 blood point for every 2 consumed. Furthermore, they take +1 level of damage from any exposure to sunlight.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Venture are the lords of the undead. Masters of not only kindred and kind, but over the night itself. While they have a twisted sense of honor, they know that they are superior and it is their right to rule others. While many have an old fashioned sense of obligation and honor, others hold to a cruel Darwinian outlook that the strong must crush over the weak. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Tremere</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Tremere/Baali: Dominate, Obfuscate, Thaumaturgy</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: Mortals with a Humanity of 4 or higher count as having +1 level of True Faith against the Tremere and mortals with a Humanity of 8 or higher receive +2 levels of True Faith. This allows a human with no True Faith to harm or repel a Tremere with holy symbols or items. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">An order of infernalists used their dark magic and pacts with demons to transform themselves into vampires. While hated and despised by many other Clans, they have managed to use their unity, ruthlessness, and dark magic to earn themselves the respect, if not the affection, of other Clans. The Clan is strictly hierarchal and it is said that the further one rises in the pyramid, the more demonic their rituals and ideology become. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Noferatu</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Nosferatu/Cappadocian: Animalism, Necromancy, Obfuscate</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: as the Nosferatu weakness, they have an Appearance of zero.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A Clan of death, the Nosferatu resemble hideously rotten corpses, though they also command powerful magics over ghosts and even death and destruction. Removed from the world of mortals and even other vampires because of their appearance, the Nosferatu practice their necromantic rituals far away from prying eyes in catacombs, sewers, ancient graveyards, and abandoned buildings. Ghosts make informants and spies without rival and this makes the Nosferatu masters of acquiring secrets and earn many favors among the kindred for this, as well as providing magical services - though despite their utility they are still feared and few other vampires endure their presence longer than they must.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Zantosa</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Toreador/Tzimisce/Giovanni: Auspex, Presence, Vicissitude</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: as the Tzimisce weakness</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Zantosa are a twisted and sadistic Clan of hedonists and flesh shapers. They use their powers to make themselves, and often their mortal slaves and playthings, beautiful beyond compare. The Zantosa love beautiful things and surround themselves with fine art, lively music, and especially beautiful mortals the sate their desires. At the heart of the Clan is the Zantosa family, an ancient family in inbred ghouls, with a number of other revenant families in their service as well. While not their primary focus, the Zantosa Clan also craves power and mastery over others, often through acquiring wealth, but even more frequently through manipulation or seduction. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Salubri</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Salubri/Ravnos/Brujah: Animalism, Auspex, Chimerstry</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: if Salubri attempt to drink the blood of an unwilling human, they must make a frenzy roll with a difficulty of 6 plus the number of blood points consumed. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Salubri a a diverse Clan of mystics, scholars, rebels, and wanderers. They have never fully been able to abide living under the rule of kings or princes and have often been involved with Anarchs or even mortal revolutions or movements for greater rights or freedoms for the lower echelons of society. As their curse makes it difficult for them to take vitae from humans by force, they have usually been one of the more humane Clans and often opposed oppression and cruelty toward humans. When they cannot influence the political landscape, they often leave and are perhaps the Clan most likely to take up nomadic lifestyles. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Gangrel</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Gangrel/Setite: Animalism, Presence, Protean</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: the Gangrel weakness</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Gangrel are in many ways closest to their animal nature, for the are masters of the wild, both of beasts and of deep and dark forests. The Gangrel are not only hunters though, they have a deep spiritual connection to primordial nature - they are the pagan priests of the vampire world and their animal magnetism draws flocks of worshippers among those mortals who makes their homes near wild places and who live in harmony with nature themselves. Like druids of old, the Gangrel lead their following in offering sacrifices of blood in sacred groves by the light of the moon. They also protect their lands and flocks, as any territorial predator might.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Malkavian</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Malkavian/Assamite: Auspex, Obfuscate, Quietus</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weakness: the Malkavian weakness</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Malkavians are a Clan of seers and madmen, much as how they are in the canon. Though perhaps even more notoriously, they are a Clan of killers. Malkavians feel a compulsion to stalk and kill, often mortals, but sometimes even their own kind. While they are feared for their madness, they are also highly desired agents and allies. They often find respect in the court of princes as spies, assassins, or agents and their insanity is tolerated as long as it can be properly directed. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T10:04:55-07:00","id":1493637,"title":"","content":"I figured that the Monsters being so close to there beasts would make resisting frenzies even harder then your &quot;normal&quot; Brujah. Still I'll probably will tweak this idea more on this cool thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T18:04:03-07:00","id":1493654,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. Anyway, here is the current rundown of your setting:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461167-combining-clans-to-get-back-to-7?p=1493637#post1493637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Followers Of Set &amp; Tremere: The outcasts of Kindred society who seek out dark and dangerous lore and practice potent and dangerous blood magics in the name of Set and other blood Gods. Yet many Kindred feel the need to make deals with them as there information gathering network and diveristy of contacts is superior to even the Nosferatu can even muster at any given time and a willing to grant with no seeming strings attached.<br /> <br /> Disciplines Spread: Auspex, Blood Sorcery, Potence and Presence.<br /> <br /> Weakness: I would keep the original weakness and maybe the Assamite Sorceror caste weakness of being unable to conceal there mystic nature.<br /> <br /> Another combo I had thought of is Banu Haqim/Ventrue: The self proclaimed rulers and judges of kindred society who feel a need to guide the other lesser clans by example and judge others by there incredibly high standards and dispose of those who are unworthy of the blood and try to curb the worst excesses of there kind as they know that humanity can wipe them out by sheer numbers and advanced weapons.<br /> <br /> Discipline spread: Auspex, Dominate Fortitude &amp; Presence:<br /> <br /> Weakness: They must feed from a specfic group of humans to avoid hunger frenzies.<br /> <br /> Another combo that is swimming around in my brain.<br /> <br /> Brujah/Gangrel: The Monsters: These Kindred are the savage monsters and slippery rebels of vampire society whom seek to tear down the foundations of the vampire ruling class. They can be savage berserkers or subtle infiltrators who worm there way into the power structure and learn the weak points and exploit it.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Celerity, Potence, Presence &amp; Protean.<br /> <br /> Weakness: The Monsters are more prone to frenzies and are at -3 to resist them and after multiple frenzies gain animalistic features subject to the storyteller's discretion.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty cool. Dark mystics in service to Set, judges of the kindred, and the beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T10:38:23-07:00","id":1493670,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m glad that you liked my other two clans. Although I felt the monsters were the best attempt at mixing clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T14:50:03-07:00","id":1494940,"title":"","content":"Okay here is another combo that I been thinking of combining. Well here goes nothing.<br /> <br /> Malkavians &amp; Ravnos (The Outcasts) This is clan is feared and respected by there insights &amp; willingness to talk truth to power and remind the other kindred that they are not infalliable and are not above to show Princes &amp; others with horrorific scenarios and curse others with there madness.<br /> <br /> Clan Discipines: Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude &amp; Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Weakness: The Outcasts share the same mental instabity as the Malkavians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T15:43:51-07:00","id":1494944,"title":"","content":"In recent times I was planning to run a DAV20 game for some friends, as I have felt in a particularly medieval mood.<br /> I was planning to tinker with the lore and homebrew some stuff to make it closer to some of my design sensibilities.<br /> One idea I had was to merge the clans back into seven. The result:<br /> <br /> The Clan of Lords(Ventrue and Lasombra).<br /> The Clan of Passion(Toreador and Brujah).<br /> The Clan of Fools(Malkavians and Ravnos).<br /> The Clan of Judges(Banu Haqim and Salubri).<br /> The Clan of Shadows(Nosferatu and Cappadocian).<br /> The Clan of the Land(Gangrel and Tzimisce).<br /> The Clan of Orphans(Caitiff).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}